Subject: [PATCH] Bound and observe DoltLite HTTP session transfers
Base: DoltLite master ffa0eafa93ab695f7863703a2cdaaa3fb7663374

This is a regenerated net patch against the state after DoltLite patches
0001-0008. The upstream master already supplies inactivity deadline refresh and
its native TLS transport; those duplicate hunks were removed after regression
evaluation. Keep the remaining fork contracts below in numbered patches and
leave the tracked upstream amalgamation and sidecars pristine.

Retained behavior:
- Keep public RemoteServer limits at 64 MiB per chunk and 128 MiB per request.
  A session-owned numeric IPv4 loopback server may accept bodies up to the
  native signed-int bound; a single Prolly chunk stays 24 bytes below it for
  hash and length framing. Permit slow body progress for this same-process
  loopback path while ordinary servers retain their request limits.
- Add request-local http_idle_timeout_ms, capped at five minutes and taking
  precedence over DOLTLITE_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS. Preserve phase-specific safe
  transport diagnostics and SQLite result codes. Allow timeout zero only for
  clear HTTP URLs with numeric IPv4 literals in 127/8.
- Add opt-in per-connection Rust callbacks for logical Dolt push chunk progress.
  Plan reachable destination-missing chunks before transfer and retain hashes
  and lengths, not payloads. Count synchronous writes on success and HTTP writes
  after the full batch succeeds.
- Retry oversized /get-chunks responses as smaller hash ranges after HTTP 413 or
  the fixed 128 MiB response bound, preserve output order, and keep a single
  overlarge chunk an error.
- Decode strict HTTP/1.1 chunked responses without Content-Length. Validate
  bounded extensions and trailers, cap encoded and decoded bodies at 128 MiB,
  and stop when the final chunk arrives even on a keepalive connection.

Cross-tree dependencies: the RemoteServer session-loopback option is consumed
by the rusqdoltlite session-owned server integration. The push callback feeds
logical chunk progress; the CBS integration separately reports physical block
progress, authorization refresh, integrity checks, and storage failures. This
patch applies to staged DoltLite sources only.

